  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) achieved 0.650 acc, a large jump over config_004 (singleprofile, scvi_n200, 0.520), confirming multiprofile + scvi_n200 as the strongest direction. However, only avgpool aggregation has been tested; transformer aggregation is unexplored. Question: Does transformer aggregation outperform avgpool for combining multiple RNA profiles with the scvi_n200 encoder? This is a clean single-variable comparison (only aggregation changes from config_005), isolating the effect of aggregation strategy. Why best next: (1) It directly extends the current best configuration along the most important untested design axis within the proven RNA-multiprofile regime. (2) The aggregation choice will propagate to all future multimodal experiments, so resolving it now reduces uncertainty for the entire remaining search. (3) It avoids the risk of simultaneously introducing image modality (which is currently very weak at ~0.21-0.23) and fusion, which would confound interpretation. (4) It is a high-information experiment: if transformer >> avgpool, we gain a clear upgrade path; if they are similar, we confirm avgpool sufficiency and can confidently move to multimodal with avgpool."
}

